## Why

- **Separate waiter:** the tab is already working, so re-sending the brief with `--wait` would make it do the work twice. This is the one case for `herdr agent wait` (§3), with the timeout set to the top of the time box.
- **Fastest ping:** the waiter is event-driven and fires the instant the tab settles. Foreground calls cap at 10 minutes and block me, and polling burns context I don't have at 58%.
- **Last week's miss:** the notice was missed because I was busy, not because background waiting failed. Nothing is queued tonight, so I stay idle and interruptible.
- **Cheap wake-up:** the output goes to a file, so the notification costs almost no context.
- **No "green":** a running agent has no result (§12). The 14/14 line is unverified and the run is unfinished, and the operator would decide whether to stay up on a number I had not checked.
- **Language:** §15 sets Russian for operator-facing text, but this session's language instruction requires English and outranks the skill, so the messages are in English.
